course: dictionary
lesson: 2001
title: Concentration: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Concentration is a word with more than one meaning. Its main meaning is giving all your attention to one thing. «Even mild dehydration can cause headaches, tiredness and poor concentration.» Headaches and tiredness are unpleasant, so poor concentration must mean finding it hard to pay attention.
explain: «Too little sleep affects mood, memory, concentration and growth.» The words around concentration are mood, memory and growth, which are things about how your body and mind work. So here concentration means how well your mind can focus. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: Context can also show you a different meaning. In science, concentration is the amount of a substance in a liquid, such as a high concentration of salt. The word looks the same, but the clues, like salt and liquid, tell you it means something else. Always check the clues.
fact: Concentration means giving all your attention to one thing.
fact: In science, concentration means the amount of a substance in a liquid or mixture: a stronger sugary solution has a higher concentration.
fact: Concentration can also mean a large number of people or things in one place, such as a concentration of shops in the town centre.
fact: Useful phrases include «lose concentration», «full concentration», «high concentration» and «concentration span».
fact: Concentration is a noun, and its plural is concentrations.
exercise: «Even mild dehydration can cause headaches, tiredness and poor concentration.» What does poor concentration mean? | Being very thirsty for water | Having lots of friends | *Finding it hard to pay attention | Feeling very happy and full of energy
exercise: In science class, Ravi says a stronger sugary drink has a high concentration. What does concentration mean here? | *The amount of sugar in the liquid | The number of children in the class | The time it takes to drink it | The colour of the cup
exercise: Teachers say «lose concentration» in class. What does that mean? | Pay for a school trip | Get a lot of attention from the teacher | Fall asleep at a concert | *Stop giving full attention to the lesson
test: Find the word that means giving your attention to one thing. | growth | mood | *concentration | sleep
test: The town centre had a concentration of shops. What does concentration mean? | Giving all your attention to a shop | A short break from work | *A large number of shops in one place | The amount of sugar in a drink
exam: «Activity makes the heart, lungs, muscles and bones stronger, and helps sleep, mood and concentration.» Which meaning of concentration fits this sentence? | *Giving all your attention to one thing | The amount of salt in water | Losing your temper | A crowd of people in one place
